Earnings quality concerns sustainability and cash support; earnings growth concerns magnitude.|Profit rises while receivables rise faster and collections stagnate.|Growth alone establishes high earnings quality?|No|Yes|Only if double-digit
Aggressive recognition records revenue before applicable performance conditions are satisfied.|Undelivered orders appear in sales despite outstanding obligations.|What should be checked first?|Contracts and transfer of control|Only share price|Only invoice font
Channel stuffing pushes excess product into distributors; round-tripping creates circular transactions without genuine substance.|A distributor receives excessive stock with broad return rights.|What weakens reported sales evidence?|Unusual returns and weak sell-through|A new packaging design|A larger warehouse alone
Improper capitalisation or deferral postpones expenses that should be recognised now.|Routine costs ₹10 are booked as assets to inflate current profit.|Current profit may be overstated by…?|Deferred costs before later charges|The cash balance alone|The share count
Reserve releases can increase profit without fresh operating performance.|A ₹5 provision is reversed without new evidence supporting the change.|What is essential?|Evidence for the revised obligation|Only higher EPS|Only management optimism
Accrual quality assesses how reliably accounting adjustments anticipate cash and reflect transactions.|Persistent earnings exceed cash because collections repeatedly fail.|What improves the investigation?|Multi-period cash and accrual reconciliation|One profit headline|One dividend announcement
Receivable and inventory growth can signal timing, credit, or demand problems; context matters.|Sales grow 10% while receivables grow 60%.|This is best treated as…?|A warning requiring investigation|Automatic proof of fraud|Proof of cash strength
Misclassification can improve CFO without changing total cash.|A cost that belongs in operating cash is placed in investing.|Total cash-flow sum necessarily changes?|No|Yes|Only if audited
Related-party dealings can move benefits away from outside owners.|A firm advances ₹20 to an owner's private entity on weak terms.|Inspect…?|Beneficiaries, terms, and recoverability|Only the announced purpose|Only nominal interest
Guarantees, leases, and funding structures may create leverage beyond headline borrowings.|₹100 reported debt excludes a material payment guarantee.|Risk assessment should include…?|Relevant contingent exposure|Only booked debt|Only cash dividends
Audit opinions indicate reporting conclusions; an emphasis paragraph highlights matters without itself modifying the opinion.|An unmodified opinion contains a going-concern emphasis under applicable circumstances.|An emphasis paragraph automatically equals an adverse opinion?|No|Yes|Only annually
Restatements correct prior reporting; control weaknesses increase error risk.|A firm revises prior revenue and identifies deficient approval controls.|What deserves follow-up?|Cause, scope, remediation, and affected periods|Only revised EPS|Only management tenure
Distress and fraud screens flag unusual patterns using statistical indicators.|A screening score flags a firm for deeper review.|Does a high-risk score prove fraud?|No|Yes|Only above a threshold
Non-GAAP metrics can aid analysis but exclusions and definitions can mislead.|A firm excludes recurring stock compensation and restructuring every year.|Best analytical response?|Reconcile and assess economic recurrence|Use adjusted profit unquestioningly|Ignore reported statements
Footnotes explain policies, estimates, exposures, and reconciliations behind headline numbers.|A debt note reveals a covenant breach hidden by a summary dashboard.|Where should investigation continue?|Debt terms and liquidity disclosures|Only the dashboard|Only the chairman's photograph
